sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Gateway as Gateway API<br/>(HTTPRoute, optional)
    participant API as Apiserver<br/>8000/TCP
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP
    participant Redis as Redis/Valkey<br/>6379/TCP
    participant S3 as S3 Object Store<br/>443/TCP
    participant Proc as Processor<br/>Worker Pool
    participant LLM as LLM Inference Gateway<br/>(vLLM / GIE/EPP)
    participant GC as GC Service

    Note over Client,LLM: Flow 1: Batch Job Submission and Processing

    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/files (upload input JSONL)<br/>X-MaaS-Username: tenant-id
    Gateway->>API: Forward request
    API->>S3: Store file content<br/>HTTPS/443, AWS IAM
    API->>PG: Create file metadata<br/>TCP/5432
    API-->>Client: 200 OK (file_id)

    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/batches<br/>X-MaaS-Username: tenant-id<br/>{input_file_id, endpoint, completion_window}
    Gateway->>API: Forward request
    API->>PG: Create batch record (status: validating)<br/>TCP/5432
    API->>S3: Download & validate input file<br/>HTTPS/443
    API->>PG: Update batch (status: in_progress)<br/>TCP/5432
    API->>Redis: Enqueue batch to priority queue (ZSET)<br/>TCP/6379
    API-->>Client: 200 OK (batch_id, status: validating)

    Note over Proc,LLM: Processor picks up job from queue

    Proc->>Redis: BZMPOP from priority queue<br/>TCP/6379
    Redis-->>Proc: batch_id (highest priority)
    Proc->>PG: Load batch metadata<br/>TCP/5432
    Proc->>S3: Download input JSONL<br/>HTTPS/443
    Proc->>Proc: Build plan file (16-byte binary entries)<br/>Group by system prompt prefix

    loop For each request in batch (AIMD concurrency control)
        Proc->>Redis: Register in-flight (HASH)<br/>TCP/6379
        Proc->>LLM: POST inference request<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, API key<br/>x-gateway-inference-objective header
        LLM-->>Proc: Inference response
        alt HTTP 429 or 5xx
            Proc->>Proc: AIMD backoff (×0.5 concurrency)
        else Success
            Proc->>Proc: AIMD additive increase (+1 slot)
        end
        Proc->>Proc: Write result to output JSONL (local emptyDir)
    end

    Proc->>S3: Upload output JSONL<br/>HTTPS/443, AWS IAM
    Proc->>PG: Create output file record<br/>TCP/5432
    Proc->>PG: Update batch (status: completed)<br/>TCP/5432
    Proc->>Redis: Remove from in-flight<br/>TCP/6379

    Note over Client,API: Flow 2: Batch Job Cancellation

    Client->>API: POST /v1/batches/{batch_id}/cancel<br/>X-MaaS-Username: tenant-id
    API->>PG: CAS update (status → cancelling)<br/>TCP/5432
    API->>Redis: Publish cancel event (LIST/BLMPop)<br/>TCP/6379
    API-->>Client: 200 OK (status: cancelling)
    Redis-->>Proc: Cancel event received
    Proc->>Proc: Context cancellation propagates
    Proc->>PG: Update batch (status: cancelled)<br/>TCP/5432

    Note over GC,S3: Flow 3: Garbage Collection & Orphan Reconciliation

    GC->>PG: Query expired batches/files<br/>TCP/5432
    PG-->>GC: Expired records
    GC->>S3: Delete expired file content<br/>HTTPS/443
    GC->>PG: Delete expired records<br/>TCP/5432

    GC->>PG: Query in_progress batches<br/>TCP/5432
    GC->>Redis: Check in-flight heartbeats (HASH)<br/>TCP/6379
    alt Stale heartbeat (no refresh within interval)
        GC->>Redis: Re-enqueue orphaned batch<br/>TCP/6379
    end
